course: dictionary
lesson: 15889
title: Uninterrupted
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Uninterrupted means going on without being stopped or broken. The prefix un- means not, and interrupted means stopped or broken into, so uninterrupted means not stopped. «She had an uninterrupted sleep, all night long without a single noise.» Nothing broke her sleep, so the word tells you it kept going.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «From the top of the tower we had an uninterrupted view of the sea.» There were no trees, hills or buildings in the way. So an uninterrupted view is one that nothing blocks.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The train made an uninterrupted journey from Leeds to London.» If you say "a journey that was not stopped", the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Uninterrupted means going on without being stopped or broken.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so uninterrupted means not interrupted.
fact: An uninterrupted view is one that nothing blocks.
fact: Uninterrupted can describe sleep, time, work, views and journeys.
exercise: «The baby had an uninterrupted sleep all night.» What does uninterrupted mean here? | *Going on without being stopped | Very noisy | Slow and tired | Broken into many small parts
exercise: «From our window we had an uninterrupted view of the mountains.» What was blocking the view? | A cloud of fog | A tall fence | The curtains | *Nothing
exercise: «The workers had uninterrupted power all day.» What does uninterrupted power mean? | Power that was very bright | *Power that never stopped | Power that was turned off | Power that was slow and weak
test: «The runners made an uninterrupted journey across the desert.» Which phrase has the same meaning as uninterrupted? | Dark and cold | *Going on without a break | Very quick | Full of people
test: «The river flowed in an uninterrupted stream past the old mill.» What does uninterrupted tell you about the river? | It was very cold | *It never stopped or was blocked | It ran backwards | It was muddy and slow
exam: Why does the writer say «an uninterrupted view of the sea»? | To show the sea was dirty | To say the view was very small | To tell us it was raining | *To show that nothing blocked the view
